# Template for .env.secrets, which is gitignored. Unlike .env, nothing here is
# copied to the deployed engine: `agents-cli deploy` reads .env only. This file is
# for values that are per-machine or must not be committed.

# Point gcloud (and anything wrapping it) at an isolated credential home instead of
# the machine-wide ~/.config/gcloud, so this project's account and quota project
# cannot be changed by, or leak into, unrelated work on the same machine.
# Create one with:
#   CLOUDSDK_CONFIG=<dir> gcloud auth login
#   CLOUDSDK_CONFIG=<dir> gcloud auth application-default login --project <project>
# CLOUDSDK_CONFIG=/home/you/.config/gcloud-<something>

# The bridge that makes the line above apply to Python too. google-auth ignores
# CLOUDSDK_CONFIG: it resolves ADC from GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, else the
# fixed ~/.config/gcloud path. Without this, gcloud uses the isolated account while
# the agent quietly authenticates as the machine-wide one — which succeeds, against
# the wrong project.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=${CLOUDSDK_CONFIG}/application_default_credentials.json
